#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gametype:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dice, Arcade"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of possible players:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Two</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; is a simple tactical game. It can played it against the computer "
"or a friend. The playing area consists of squares containing points. When "
"the game starts each square has only one point, and no owner. Players move "
"by clicking on either a vacant square, or on own square, thus increasing the "
"square’s point value. Once the square’s value reaches maximum the excessive "
"points are distributed around the neighboring squares conquering them. The "
"winner is the player who ends up owning all the squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Objective:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Conquer all the squares on the game board to win the round."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; loads directly into the game mode, so you can start playing right "
"away."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You move by clicking on a vacant square or the one you already own. If you "
"click on a vacant square, you gain an ownership over it and square’s color "
"changes to your playing color. Each time you click on a square, the value of "
"the square increases by one. If square's value reaches maximum, its points "
"are distributed amongst the square’s immediate neighbors (the points ‘jump’ "
"around). If a neighboring square happens to be owned by the other player, it "
"gets taken over together with all of its points and changes color to your "
"playing color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a square in the centre reaches five points, four of its points go to its "
"four neighbors leaving the source square with a single point. It is possible "
"for a cascade of automatic moves to occur if the neighboring squares also "
"reach a maximum due to the points’ distribution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Note:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Large parts of the playing area can change hands very rapidly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The winner is the player who ends up owning all the squares on the board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules, Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A move consists of clicking on a square that does not belong to your "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "The move increases the points in the square by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the start of the game, each square has one point, is painted a neutral "
"color and has no owner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each player has a color to mark ownership of squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking a square that has no owner, player becomes the owner of that "
"square and it changes its color to player's color. Simultaneously the "
"square’s value is increased by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a square has more points than it has neighbors, one point jumps to each "
"of the neighbors, leaving only one point in the original square."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During such a move, all the neighboring squares become owned by the player "
"who moved and so do all of their points, even if the neighbors were neutral "
"or owned by the other player before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Neighbors are the squares above, below, left and right, but not any "
"diagonally located squares. Corner squares have only two neighbors, while "
"side squares have three, and centre squares have four neighbors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a move leaves a neighbor with a maximum number of points, the move "
"continues automatically to the neighbor's neighbors and so on, in a cascade. "
"A large number of squares can change ownership during such a move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "The winner is the player who ends up owning all the squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"&kappname;</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to select colors, computer player, "
"skill level and board size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to avoid increasing a square when your opponent owns a neighboring "
"square that can reach its maximum before your square does."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to get control of the corner squares first, then the side squares. You "
"need fewer moves to make them reach a maximum."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try not to play too close to your opponent, especially during the opening "
"moves. Drop back a square or two or pick a square on the diagonal from your "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep an eye out for long chains of squares that are almost at their maximum. "
"If they are yours, you must guard them against cascading moves. If they are "
"your opponent's, they can become ripe for capture by a cascading move, just "
"as soon as they extend close enough to your territory."
msgstr ""

